<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Attalus III</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 170–133 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Attalus III was the last Attalid king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pergamon">Pergamon</a>, reigning from 138 BCE. On his death in 133 BCE he left his kingdom to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in his will. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aristonicus">Aristonicus</a>, claiming to be a royal son, led a revolt against the bequest, but by 129 BCE the kingdom had become the Roman province of Asia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/attalus-iii.jpg" alt="Attalus III" width="320" height="409" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Marcus Cyron · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Attalid_portrait_at_the_Antikensammlung_Berlin.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
